1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:05,400
Characters, actions, places, occupations,
and events in this series

2
00:00:05,430 --> 00:00:08,070
are fictional and created
for entertainment purposes only.

3
00:00:08,090 --> 00:00:12,270
They are not intended to urge
or promote any behavior in the series.

4
00:00:12,300 --> 00:00:14,610
Viewer discretion is advised.

5
00:00:14,630 --> 00:00:16,290
I’ve got something to tell you.

6
00:00:16,770 --> 00:00:18,230
Mom… died many years ago.

7
00:00:18,250 --> 00:00:19,920
Tomorrow, I’m taking Lookpeach
to visit her.

8
00:00:19,940 --> 00:00:23,270
After all, she gave me
the most precious person in my life.

9
00:00:23,290 --> 00:00:26,600
She also… gave me
the most precious person in my life.

10
00:00:26,750 --> 00:00:28,200
We don’t owe each other anything anymore.

11
00:00:28,230 --> 00:00:29,490
I’m not angry with you anymore.

12
00:00:29,510 --> 00:00:30,300
Mr. Thee!

13
00:00:31,320 --> 00:00:33,090
Don’t ever do this again in my territory.

14
00:00:33,110 --> 00:00:34,570
I won’t stand by
and watch Mok get hurt like that again.

15
00:00:34,590 --> 00:00:36,050
Mr. Rome isn’t cruel.

16
00:00:36,090 --> 00:00:37,450
He just loves Mr. Mok that much.

17
00:00:37,490 --> 00:00:38,010
I’m sorry.

18
00:00:38,100 --> 00:00:39,200
I’m sorry too.

19
00:00:39,230 --> 00:00:40,490
These two can never
stay mad at each other for long.

20
00:00:41,430 --> 00:00:42,730
I thought you were going back
to Hong Kong.

21
00:00:42,750 --> 00:00:44,000
After Mok’s fully recovered.

22
00:00:44,250 --> 00:00:45,570
There’s a series script
and a casting call.

23
00:00:45,640 --> 00:00:47,130
You think the title sounds familiar?

24
00:00:55,350 --> 00:00:58,400
We can all tell
Peach planned this trip for me.

25
00:01:01,400 --> 00:01:02,100
What?

26
00:01:03,320 --> 00:01:04,800
Quit making that sad puppy face.

27
00:01:05,170 --> 00:01:07,170
Peach might say it’s adorable.

28
00:01:07,560 --> 00:01:08,800
To everyone else,

29
00:01:09,590 --> 00:01:12,400
you just look like an old man
trying to be cute.

30
00:01:12,670 --> 00:01:13,200
Rome!

31
00:01:13,410 --> 00:01:16,410
And whenever he calls you cute,
don’t buy it.

32
00:01:16,750 --> 00:01:18,850
Everyone else doesn’t find you cute, Kian.

33
00:01:19,710 --> 00:01:21,200
Hey! Come on.

34
00:01:21,810 --> 00:01:23,210
At least we get two separate tents.

35
00:01:24,950 --> 00:01:25,700
Wait…

36
00:01:26,110 --> 00:01:27,400
Should all four of us share one?

37
00:01:29,420 --> 00:01:30,200
Fine.

38
00:01:30,450 --> 00:01:32,600
I get to cuddle Lookpeach
to sleep every night.

39
00:01:33,390 --> 00:01:35,100
Skipping it for one night

40
00:01:35,820 --> 00:01:37,100
won’t be the death of me.

41
00:01:38,460 --> 00:01:39,800
Unlike someone…

42
00:01:40,640 --> 00:01:42,810
who’s been waiting
for his partner’s injury to heal.

43
00:01:43,039 --> 00:01:44,800
No bedroom action for a whole week.

44
00:01:47,070 --> 00:01:48,400
He’s about to writhe around

45
00:01:49,030 --> 00:01:50,400
like an upside-down cockroach.

46
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:54,300
Kian, come on.

47
00:01:54,600 --> 00:01:56,500
If I don’t get to cuddle Mok tonight,

48
00:01:57,270 --> 00:01:59,150
I’ll perish before I ever
take over as leader.

49
00:02:00,150 --> 00:02:01,000
Please, please.

50
00:02:03,340 --> 00:02:04,100
Hey.

51
00:02:04,680 --> 00:02:06,700
Challenge me to a shooting match
or a horse race.

52
00:02:07,350 --> 00:02:09,530
But don’t you dare
compete with me in love.

53
00:02:11,620 --> 00:02:12,400
Yes, sir.

54
00:02:13,860 --> 00:02:14,850
See this?

55
00:02:15,980 --> 00:02:18,200
You don’t even have
a defined relationship.

56
00:02:18,920 --> 00:02:20,940
We’re playing in
completely different leagues.

57
00:02:21,540 --> 00:02:22,400
Got it?

58
00:02:23,320 --> 00:02:26,380
Once we head back to our own tents,

59
00:02:26,570 --> 00:02:28,200
whatever you hear,

60
00:02:29,180 --> 00:02:30,100
don’t ask questions.

61
00:02:31,010 --> 00:02:32,250
Don’t eavesdrop.

62
00:02:35,579 --> 00:02:36,250
Deal.

63
00:02:36,460 --> 00:02:37,230
Dude.

64
00:02:44,240 --> 00:02:45,690
I wonder what they’re talking about.

65
00:02:46,990 --> 00:02:48,200
They look adorable.

66
00:02:48,320 --> 00:02:49,600
I bet it’s something nice.

67
00:04:01,980 --> 00:04:02,600
Mira.

68
00:04:03,880 --> 00:04:04,480
Ow!

69
00:04:07,290 --> 00:04:08,100
Ms. Plub!

70
00:04:10,860 --> 00:04:11,750
I’m sorry.

71
00:04:20,190 --> 00:04:21,700
My lunch…

72
00:04:32,650 --> 00:04:33,800
Drink this to tide you over.

73
00:04:34,040 --> 00:04:34,880
Thank you.

74
00:04:48,420 --> 00:04:50,490
Why didn’t you go camping
with everyone else?

75
00:04:52,050 --> 00:04:54,490
I was ordered to stay behind
and clear some paperwork at the office.

76
00:04:54,800 --> 00:04:58,780
Mr. Mok alone is worth
a whole team of bodyguards.

77
00:04:59,560 --> 00:05:02,880
Someone with his skills
is hard to come by.

78
00:05:04,310 --> 00:05:05,300
You, Mira.

79
00:05:06,580 --> 00:05:07,300
Yes?

80
00:05:07,920 --> 00:05:09,730
Dad sent you to replace Mr. Mok.

81
00:05:09,950 --> 00:05:12,900
That means he trusts you
just as much as he trusts him.

82
00:05:13,880 --> 00:05:15,730
ARSENI has branches all over the world.

83
00:05:16,210 --> 00:05:20,100
Getting transferred is normal.

84
00:05:20,640 --> 00:05:22,930
No explanations. Just orders.

85
00:05:25,530 --> 00:05:29,500
Everyone wants to be
Mr. Theerakit’s right-hand man.

86
00:05:31,530 --> 00:05:33,400
But Dad chose you.

87
00:05:33,930 --> 00:05:35,000
That means…

88
00:05:35,050 --> 00:05:36,000
That means…

89
00:05:36,890 --> 00:05:40,200
ARSENI Thailand, under Mr. Theerakit,

90
00:05:40,750 --> 00:05:42,290
stands apart from every other branch.

91
00:05:42,850 --> 00:05:43,850
No weapons.

92
00:05:44,450 --> 00:05:45,470
No enemies.

93
00:05:45,570 --> 00:05:46,500
No black.

94
00:05:48,090 --> 00:05:53,090
Being assigned here doesn’t mean
I’m as capable as Mr. Mok.

95
00:05:54,300 --> 00:05:57,500
It just means they don’t need
someone with exceptional skills.

96
00:05:58,840 --> 00:06:00,900
Why do you sell yourself short like that?

97
00:06:04,820 --> 00:06:05,970
As far as I’m concerned,

98
00:06:06,560 --> 00:06:09,300
you’re more than capable of being here.

99
00:06:12,400 --> 00:06:13,300
Thank you.

100
00:06:13,580 --> 00:06:16,100
But Mr. Mok is still helping me
with a lot of things.

101
00:06:16,310 --> 00:06:17,300
It’s too early to judge.

102
00:06:18,020 --> 00:06:21,370
The real test will be
when Mr. Kritdanai takes over

103
00:06:21,960 --> 00:06:23,200
and Mr. Mok returns to Hong Kong.

104
00:06:24,300 --> 00:06:28,900
That’s when we’ll find out
if I’m really as capable as you say.

105
00:06:30,850 --> 00:06:32,159
I’m sure you’ll do just fine.

106
00:06:42,110 --> 00:06:42,900
Mira.

107
00:06:43,740 --> 00:06:45,000
Can I ask you something?

108
00:06:45,830 --> 00:06:47,400
If I have the answer.

109
00:06:50,990 --> 00:06:57,000
Why is Rome taking over instead of Thee?

110
00:07:02,020 --> 00:07:03,800
Because that’s what Mr. Theerakit wants.

111
00:07:04,570 --> 00:07:06,800
He doesn’t want to lead ARSENI.

112
00:07:08,020 --> 00:07:10,400
What if Rome doesn’t want it either?

113
00:07:11,500 --> 00:07:12,700
What will Dad do?

114
00:07:13,380 --> 00:07:15,000
There’s no Plan B for that.

115
00:07:16,560 --> 00:07:19,500
Master knows that’s never going to happen.

116
00:07:20,570 --> 00:07:23,300
As far as I can remember,
Mr. Thee likes to negotiate.

117
00:07:23,600 --> 00:07:26,530
Mr. Rome prefers to settle things
with his fists.

118
00:07:27,010 --> 00:07:29,980
The two of them
couldn’t be more different.

119
00:07:31,400 --> 00:07:32,380
Which means…

120
00:07:34,560 --> 00:07:37,100
the successor was never changed.

121
00:07:37,290 --> 00:07:39,800
Dad knew from the beginning
it’d be Mr. Rome,

122
00:07:40,710 --> 00:07:41,600
not Mr. Thee.

123
00:07:42,840 --> 00:07:44,100
Everyone knows it.

124
00:07:45,550 --> 00:07:47,050
They just don’t say it out loud.

125
00:07:50,360 --> 00:07:52,200
Mr. Rome is a better fit in every way.

126
00:07:54,409 --> 00:07:55,870
Not because Mr. Thee isn’t capable,

127
00:07:56,560 --> 00:08:01,800
but because he’s too kind…
for the position.

128
00:08:03,300 --> 00:08:06,490
Are you trying to comfort me,
or did Mr. Thee tell you to say that?

129
00:08:08,610 --> 00:08:09,900
I was fired.

130
00:08:10,970 --> 00:08:13,000
Why would I still be
taking orders from him?

131
00:08:17,290 --> 00:08:20,830
Everything happens for a reason

132
00:08:22,700 --> 00:08:26,000
and it’s all been decided.

133
00:08:26,560 --> 00:08:28,250
You don’t have to feel guilty, Mr. Peach.

134
00:08:30,890 --> 00:08:34,200
I’m telling you this today

135
00:08:35,860 --> 00:08:39,299
because I don’t want to leave
anything unsaid before I go.

136
00:08:41,210 --> 00:08:43,400
With or without you,

137
00:08:44,330 --> 00:08:46,650
Mr. Thee was never
going to become ARSENI’s leader.

138
00:08:48,310 --> 00:08:49,300
You just happen to be…

139
00:08:50,210 --> 00:08:53,900
one of the best things in Mr. Thee’s life.

140
00:09:00,780 --> 00:09:01,800
From now on,

141
00:09:03,830 --> 00:09:05,200
please take good care of Mr. Thee.

142
00:09:06,330 --> 00:09:08,200
With pleasure. For the rest of my life.

143
00:09:12,400 --> 00:09:13,300
You too, Mr. Mok.

144
00:09:15,580 --> 00:09:16,900
Live a very happy life.

145
00:09:21,890 --> 00:09:24,500
After I go back this time,
I don’t know when I’ll get to play again.

146
00:09:24,920 --> 00:09:25,700
No.

147
00:09:26,550 --> 00:09:29,100
I don’t know
if I’ll ever get to play at all.

148
00:09:29,740 --> 00:09:32,300
Don’t let anything make you lose yourself.

149
00:09:39,090 --> 00:09:40,000
Do you think…

150
00:09:41,310 --> 00:09:45,450
being ARSENI’s leader is hard?

151
00:09:46,700 --> 00:09:47,170
Yes.

152
00:09:47,240 --> 00:09:47,980
What?

153
00:09:48,890 --> 00:09:50,200
You’re supposed to say it’s not.

154
00:09:51,130 --> 00:09:51,850
Encourage me.

155
00:09:51,960 --> 00:09:53,800
But I believe you’ll be a good leader.

156
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:56,700
Okay.

157
00:10:00,210 --> 00:10:01,900
Just don’t forget your promise.

158
00:10:02,890 --> 00:10:04,130
You have to stay and help me.

159
00:10:08,660 --> 00:10:10,900
Whenever you feel like playing,
just come back here.

160
00:10:11,690 --> 00:10:13,400
And whenever you need help,

161
00:10:13,840 --> 00:10:16,700
I promise I’ll be the first one there.

162
00:10:35,710 --> 00:10:36,460
Ouch!

163
00:10:36,510 --> 00:10:37,320
Damn it, Kian!

164
00:10:37,730 --> 00:10:41,100
As ARSENI’s future leader,
this isn’t gonna kill you.

165
00:10:41,950 --> 00:10:42,520
Ow!

166
00:10:48,020 --> 00:10:49,500
Just let the fire burn out.

167
00:10:49,720 --> 00:10:51,500
I forgot we’re not in winter.

168
00:10:52,190 --> 00:10:53,000
It’s fine.

169
00:10:53,980 --> 00:10:54,990
It sets da mood.

170
00:11:04,310 --> 00:11:06,040
What are you doing? You’re making a mess.

171
00:11:11,430 --> 00:11:12,500
Hold still.

172
00:11:14,280 --> 00:11:15,400
Look at you. It’s all dirty.

173
00:11:15,630 --> 00:11:18,850
Roger that, love of my life.

174
00:11:19,900 --> 00:11:20,560
Yuck!

175
00:11:21,210 --> 00:11:21,900
Ew!

176
00:11:39,320 --> 00:11:40,050
Mok.

177
00:11:40,890 --> 00:11:41,800
Is there something on my face?

178
00:11:41,850 --> 00:11:42,440
No.

179
00:11:43,460 --> 00:11:44,200
What?

180
00:11:44,590 --> 00:11:47,200
-You’re supposed to say it’s dirty.
-Then you can wipe it off yourself.

181
00:11:51,140 --> 00:11:51,800
Huh.

182
00:11:52,990 --> 00:11:56,380
Even a stray dog looks
less pathetic than you right now.

183
00:11:59,060 --> 00:12:00,250
Quit picking on your brother.

184
00:12:00,990 --> 00:12:01,900
I’m just telling the truth.

185
00:12:03,810 --> 00:12:05,210
Come here. I’ll clean your face.

186
00:12:06,160 --> 00:12:06,800
Yes!

187
00:12:07,480 --> 00:12:08,700
You’re the best, Peach.

188
00:12:12,450 --> 00:12:13,180
Right here.

189
00:12:14,970 --> 00:12:16,120
It’s me!

190
00:12:16,550 --> 00:12:17,510
How’s that?

191
00:12:17,530 --> 00:12:18,500
Kian, what are you doing?

192
00:12:18,530 --> 00:12:19,390
Why so rough?

193
00:12:19,420 --> 00:12:20,310
The other side too.

194
00:12:20,320 --> 00:12:21,580
-One side’s enough.
-Let me help.

195
00:12:21,600 --> 00:12:23,300
One side’s enough! Peach, help me!

196
00:12:23,470 --> 00:12:24,100
Mok!

197
00:12:27,690 --> 00:12:29,300
We were in the shower for a few minutes,

198
00:12:29,640 --> 00:12:31,100
and they’d already turned in.

199
00:12:39,260 --> 00:12:40,130
Why are you smiling?

200
00:12:41,510 --> 00:12:42,300
Oh, no.

201
00:12:43,340 --> 00:12:44,600
Am I smiling?

202
00:12:48,930 --> 00:12:52,090
Let’s go soak up the atmosphere
and leave them here…

203
00:12:53,480 --> 00:12:55,250
to enjoy their honeymoon.

204
00:12:55,820 --> 00:12:56,700
Hmm?

205
00:12:58,730 --> 00:13:00,290
I’m going to cuddle Mok all night.

206
00:13:00,440 --> 00:13:02,600
Just thinking about it
makes me want to go to bed already.

207
00:13:03,260 --> 00:13:04,220
Easy there.

208
00:13:04,500 --> 00:13:06,400
You and Mok aren’t even official yet.

209
00:13:08,320 --> 00:13:09,800
Don’t start acting old-fashioned, bro.

210
00:13:10,030 --> 00:13:13,890
According to Mom, you and Peach
skipped a few steps yourselves.

211
00:13:15,020 --> 00:13:16,300
-Rome.
-Oh, come on.

212
00:13:17,040 --> 00:13:18,500
I know you’re protective of your friend,

213
00:13:18,750 --> 00:13:22,100
but you see
we’ve been in love for ten years.

214
00:13:22,820 --> 00:13:23,650
Don’t you trust me?

215
00:13:25,020 --> 00:13:26,380
That’s not the point.

216
00:13:27,360 --> 00:13:29,050
The point is his consent.

217
00:13:29,470 --> 00:13:30,300
Don’t force him.

218
00:13:30,520 --> 00:13:31,500
Don’t pressure him.

219
00:13:32,500 --> 00:13:34,100
Don’t go against his wishes.

220
00:13:34,220 --> 00:13:35,000
Please.

221
00:13:35,650 --> 00:13:38,380
Mok will definitely say yes.

222
00:13:38,700 --> 00:13:39,580
One hundred percent sure.

223
00:13:47,310 --> 00:13:48,650
Let’s go, dumpling.

224
00:13:58,000 --> 00:13:59,300
Why are you glued to me like this?

225
00:14:01,800 --> 00:14:03,130
Well, the tent’s tiny.

226
00:14:03,940 --> 00:14:05,000
And that empty space?

227
00:14:05,860 --> 00:14:07,010
Saving it for a ghost?

228
00:14:08,600 --> 00:14:11,130
Hey, we’re in the middle of the woods.
Don’t talk about ghosts.

229
00:14:11,670 --> 00:14:13,290
It’s scary. Gosh.

230
00:14:15,580 --> 00:14:18,490
Could someone like you
be scared of anything?

231
00:14:20,490 --> 00:14:21,200
Hm?

232
00:14:22,150 --> 00:14:23,330
I used to be fearless.

233
00:14:23,800 --> 00:14:26,640
But I’m not anymore.

234
00:14:30,800 --> 00:14:31,650
What are you scared of now?

235
00:14:34,820 --> 00:14:35,700
You.

236
00:14:35,970 --> 00:14:36,720
Me?

237
00:14:38,600 --> 00:14:39,800
I’m scared you won’t love me.

238
00:14:43,360 --> 00:14:44,100
Then…

239
00:14:45,830 --> 00:14:47,730
go back to being fearless.

240
00:14:48,940 --> 00:14:49,700
Hm?

241
00:14:50,990 --> 00:14:54,300
Because there’s never been a day
I didn’t love you.

242
00:14:57,960 --> 00:15:00,300
Are you making a love confession?

243
00:15:02,840 --> 00:15:03,850
Interpret it however you want.

244
00:15:14,650 --> 00:15:15,850
Those aren’t exactly tight lips.

245
00:15:20,940 --> 00:15:22,300
Anything you want to do

246
00:15:22,930 --> 00:15:24,410
before we head back to Hong Kong
tomorrow morning?

247
00:15:25,920 --> 00:15:26,900
Mm…

248
00:15:28,540 --> 00:15:29,300
There is.

249
00:15:30,510 --> 00:15:31,300
What is it?

250
00:15:32,310 --> 00:15:33,200
I want to…

251
00:15:36,440 --> 00:15:37,400
love you.

252
00:16:00,630 --> 00:16:01,400
That’s Polaris.

253
00:16:02,510 --> 00:16:04,010
In Thai, it’s called Dao Nuea.

254
00:16:04,160 --> 00:16:07,770
Trekkers used it
to find their way at night.

255
00:16:12,170 --> 00:16:14,200
And over there is the Pleiades.

256
00:16:15,110 --> 00:16:16,780
In Thai, they’re called Dao Lookkai.

257
00:16:17,030 --> 00:16:20,690
Back then, farmers used them to tell
when it was time to plant or harvest.

258
00:16:21,040 --> 00:16:23,980
Nowadays, we’ve got technology.

259
00:16:24,130 --> 00:16:27,400
The stars are just
something beautiful to admire.

260
00:16:27,520 --> 00:16:28,450
Impressive.

261
00:16:29,220 --> 00:16:31,130
You know a lot about stars.

262
00:16:33,880 --> 00:16:35,000
Oh, that’s not all.

263
00:16:35,300 --> 00:16:37,500
If you’re about to make
another Peachayarat Star joke,

264
00:16:38,490 --> 00:16:39,400
don’t.

265
00:16:39,750 --> 00:16:41,500
I already told you it’s not real.

266
00:16:52,890 --> 00:16:53,600
Shit!

267
00:16:56,950 --> 00:16:58,330
They’re not the Peachayarat Stars.

268
00:16:58,720 --> 00:17:00,500
They’re the Lookpeach Constellation.

269
00:17:00,700 --> 00:17:02,090
And their sole purpose…

270
00:17:02,780 --> 00:17:05,130
is to bear witness to how much I love you.

271
00:17:05,599 --> 00:17:09,579
They’ll stay there until the end of time.

272
00:17:11,020 --> 00:17:12,599
So that whole astronomy lesson

273
00:17:12,950 --> 00:17:14,490
was just building up to your surprise?

274
00:17:23,329 --> 00:17:24,200
P’Kian…

275
00:17:25,020 --> 00:17:26,130
How did you even do this?

276
00:17:28,380 --> 00:17:30,500
Creating a constellation is nothing.

277
00:17:30,720 --> 00:17:35,600
I’d gift-wrap the entire universe
and give it to you,

278
00:17:37,550 --> 00:17:39,000
if that’s what you want.

279
00:17:41,110 --> 00:17:42,500
Who on earth did I marry?

280
00:17:43,990 --> 00:17:45,490
Theerakit Kian Lee.

281
00:17:47,320 --> 00:17:49,180
The man whose last name you’re using.

282
00:17:55,320 --> 00:17:56,300
Thanks a lot, Mira.

283
00:17:56,870 --> 00:18:00,500
Is Theerakit Kian Lee ever going to stop?

284
00:18:01,350 --> 00:18:03,300
Until sugar forgets how to be sweet.

285
00:18:03,580 --> 00:18:05,210
Until salt forgets how to be salty.

286
00:18:05,390 --> 00:18:07,500
Until diamonds fall from the sky
instead of raindrops.

287
00:18:09,770 --> 00:18:10,800
That’s the day…

288
00:18:12,560 --> 00:18:13,890
I’ll stop loving you.

289
00:18:15,680 --> 00:18:17,310
You could’ve just said, “Never.”

290
00:18:18,970 --> 00:18:24,900
Even if salt turns sweet
and sugar turns sour,

291
00:18:26,460 --> 00:18:29,600
I’ll never stop loving you, P’Kian.

292
00:18:32,950 --> 00:18:33,700
Lookpeach…

293
00:18:34,430 --> 00:18:35,400
What are you even saying?

294
00:18:37,550 --> 00:18:39,100
You’re getting bolder every day.

295
00:18:41,330 --> 00:18:43,180
Sure, I have muscles this big

296
00:18:44,600 --> 00:18:48,400
but my heart is this tiny.

297
00:18:49,660 --> 00:18:51,210
How can a heart be that tiny?

298
00:18:53,710 --> 00:18:58,700
It’s just big enough
to pump blood through my body.

299
00:18:59,940 --> 00:19:01,800
As for love…

300
00:19:03,100 --> 00:19:04,900
I already gave
every last bit of it to you,

301
00:19:05,860 --> 00:19:07,400
center of my universe.

302
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:18,500
Do you enjoy this trip, P’Kian?

303
00:19:24,960 --> 00:19:26,800
Why did you bring us here?

304
00:19:27,420 --> 00:19:30,100
I could see it in your eyes
when you talked about camping.

305
00:19:31,120 --> 00:19:35,530
Yours, Mr. Rome’s, and Mr. Mok’s.

306
00:19:36,320 --> 00:19:37,700
You three couldn’t stop talking about it.

307
00:19:39,750 --> 00:19:42,100
It must be something very special.

308
00:19:43,610 --> 00:19:47,700
So I figured this’d be
better than a hotel stay.

309
00:19:50,960 --> 00:19:52,780
Even after all these years,

310
00:19:54,670 --> 00:19:57,100
I still remember
how happy we were back then.

311
00:19:58,100 --> 00:19:59,100
No worries.

312
00:20:01,790 --> 00:20:03,100
No pressure.

313
00:20:06,750 --> 00:20:08,100
No burdens.

314
00:20:12,470 --> 00:20:13,800
Just having fun.

315
00:20:16,470 --> 00:20:21,290
Mr. Mok told me
that living an ordinary life,

316
00:20:22,100 --> 00:20:23,200
without bodyguards,

317
00:20:24,650 --> 00:20:26,100
or a convoy,

318
00:20:27,520 --> 00:20:29,980
is the birthday gift
Mr. Rome wishes for every year.

319
00:20:33,320 --> 00:20:35,400
So I wanted to give him that
before he leaves.

320
00:20:36,500 --> 00:20:39,000
This trip will be a memory we’ll treasure.

321
00:20:41,430 --> 00:20:42,560
Especially Rome.

322
00:20:49,620 --> 00:20:50,800
You’re the right person.

323
00:20:52,370 --> 00:20:53,650
The best choice ever.

324
00:20:55,180 --> 00:20:55,900
Hmm?

325
00:20:58,150 --> 00:20:59,700
You don’t just love me.

326
00:21:02,560 --> 00:21:05,400
You love everyone around me too.

327
00:21:07,430 --> 00:21:09,400
That’s how I know

328
00:21:10,070 --> 00:21:11,300
you’re the one.

329
00:21:14,530 --> 00:21:15,800
The only one for me, Lookpeach.

330
00:21:23,310 --> 00:21:23,980
Hey.

331
00:21:25,210 --> 00:21:26,500
What are you doing?

332
00:21:29,760 --> 00:21:34,100
I know you planned this trip for Rome,

333
00:21:35,510 --> 00:21:40,330
but don’t forget
you also called it our honeymoon.

334
00:21:44,390 --> 00:21:47,300
I was just saying that.

335
00:21:49,440 --> 00:21:50,380
No way.

336
00:21:52,090 --> 00:21:53,600
With Theerakit Kian Lee,

337
00:21:54,910 --> 00:21:56,600
you don’t say things you don’t mean

338
00:21:57,520 --> 00:21:59,100
or make promises you can’t keep.

339
00:22:03,900 --> 00:22:05,400
So what do I have to do…

340
00:22:05,940 --> 00:22:08,100
to satisfy Theerakit Kian Lee?

341
00:22:10,400 --> 00:22:11,500
Hmm…

342
00:22:14,260 --> 00:22:18,530
What do people usually do
on their honeymoon?

343
00:22:26,540 --> 00:22:27,330
I think that’s enough.

344
00:22:27,370 --> 00:22:28,200
It’s not.

345
00:22:29,050 --> 00:22:31,300
Nowhere near what I’d call a honeymoon.

346
00:22:32,790 --> 00:22:34,400
If that’s all you’re giving me,

347
00:22:35,480 --> 00:22:37,400
you’d better keep going

348
00:22:38,550 --> 00:22:41,010
until the sun comes up on the horizon.

349
00:22:51,290 --> 00:22:52,400
I told you

350
00:22:53,040 --> 00:22:54,530
if this is all you’re going to do,

351
00:22:54,680 --> 00:22:55,600
then you’ll have to…

352
00:23:21,590 --> 00:23:22,300
-Dad.
-Dad.

353
00:23:29,800 --> 00:23:32,200
Dad and I bought you guys
a bunch of snacks.

354
00:23:32,760 --> 00:23:33,700
Did you miss me?

355
00:23:33,910 --> 00:23:34,780
We did.

356
00:23:37,980 --> 00:23:40,300
Where’s Uncle Rome?

357
00:23:41,940 --> 00:23:42,720
And Mok?

358
00:23:42,750 --> 00:23:44,290
Didn’t you all come back together?

359
00:23:47,980 --> 00:23:50,500
(Didn’t you say you still had time?)

360
00:23:51,460 --> 00:23:53,290
Why are you leaving at the crack of dawn?

361
00:23:54,630 --> 00:23:56,300
We did have time, but only for one night.

362
00:23:56,780 --> 00:24:00,610
Mr. Rome has to report for duty
in Hong Kong later this morning.

363
00:24:00,940 --> 00:24:02,100
The car’s ready.

364
00:24:02,670 --> 00:24:03,890
You don’t have to worry.

365
00:24:04,020 --> 00:24:05,600
You two can go back to sleep.

366
00:24:06,790 --> 00:24:08,000
If everything’s settled,

367
00:24:09,310 --> 00:24:10,600
I guess this is goodbye.

368
00:24:14,650 --> 00:24:15,580
-Hold on.
-Wait.

369
00:24:34,200 --> 00:24:37,180
Our secret deal stands.

370
00:24:38,160 --> 00:24:39,850
(Getting transferred here…)

371
00:24:40,920 --> 00:24:43,450
…isn’t nearly as hard as
losing a friend like you.
FIRST YEAR IN THAILAND

372
00:24:43,480 --> 00:24:44,570
-Boss.
-Hey.

373
00:24:44,670 --> 00:24:46,780
You promised you could be both.

374
00:24:47,280 --> 00:24:48,300
My right-hand man…

375
00:24:49,640 --> 00:24:50,850
and my friend.

376
00:24:51,050 --> 00:24:52,440
I’m sorry I couldn’t keep that promise.

377
00:24:52,470 --> 00:24:53,900
Mok, come on.

378
00:25:01,530 --> 00:25:04,700
Master’s people are listening
through the earpiece.

379
00:25:06,340 --> 00:25:09,580
If I disobey the order,
I might get transferred

380
00:25:11,170 --> 00:25:13,000
and you’ll really be on your own.

381
00:25:17,950 --> 00:25:19,210
Dad really went that far?

382
00:25:19,910 --> 00:25:21,250
Until everyone here trusts me.

383
00:25:23,410 --> 00:25:26,700
But I can switch
this earpiece off sometimes.

384
00:25:28,080 --> 00:25:29,700
Just for a little while.

385
00:25:36,750 --> 00:25:38,200
Then we’ll be friends again

386
00:25:39,890 --> 00:25:42,100
whenever you turn it off, even for a bit.

387
00:25:50,090 --> 00:25:51,100
Our secret deal.

388
00:25:54,800 --> 00:25:57,610
Take care, Boss.

389
00:26:01,180 --> 00:26:02,600
So that’s the last time

390
00:26:04,360 --> 00:26:09,140
I’ll hear that word from you, huh, Mok?

391
00:26:19,220 --> 00:26:20,380
I’m just glad…

392
00:26:21,760 --> 00:26:23,410
we’re friends again, man.

393
00:26:25,700 --> 00:26:27,000
Me too,

394
00:26:29,750 --> 00:26:30,450
buddy.

395
00:26:54,780 --> 00:26:56,200
(We’ve landed in Hong Kong.)

396
00:26:56,510 --> 00:26:58,090
When are you coming back, Uncle Rome?

397
00:26:58,120 --> 00:26:59,400
I miss you already.

398
00:26:59,540 --> 00:27:00,250
Come on.

399
00:27:00,480 --> 00:27:02,800
We literally just landed,
and you already miss us?

400
00:27:03,570 --> 00:27:04,400
Isn’t that a little too soon?

401
00:27:04,580 --> 00:27:05,810
I want to visit Hong Kong.

402
00:27:05,940 --> 00:27:06,600
Come on over.

403
00:27:06,820 --> 00:27:07,900
I’ll be your personal tour guide.

404
00:27:08,560 --> 00:27:09,890
Mom misses you so much.

405
00:27:20,490 --> 00:27:21,400
Busy with work?

406
00:27:22,770 --> 00:27:23,900
I’m going over the schedule

407
00:27:23,920 --> 00:27:26,700
for Me and Thee’s first day
of filming tomorrow.

408
00:27:27,940 --> 00:27:29,490
That reminds me.
I wanted to ask you something.

409
00:27:30,010 --> 00:27:30,770
Yes?

410
00:27:32,420 --> 00:27:34,780
Do you want to go watch
our story together?

411
00:27:47,190 --> 00:27:49,600
You can’t open it
with your hand hurting like that.

412
00:28:05,850 --> 00:28:06,700
Thank you.

413
00:28:09,740 --> 00:28:11,610
That’s what happens when you
stick your nose where it doesn’t belong.

414
00:28:19,100 --> 00:28:20,380
If it hurts, just cry.

415
00:28:21,370 --> 00:28:22,930
Why are you pretending to be strong?

416
00:28:23,980 --> 00:28:27,700
It doesn’t make me
want to admire you more.

417
00:28:29,700 --> 00:28:31,500
Well, it doesn’t hurt.

418
00:28:32,200 --> 00:28:33,100
Why would I cry?

419
00:28:47,250 --> 00:28:48,330
What do you think you’re doing?

420
00:28:53,220 --> 00:28:58,500
My breath will ease the pain
you’re going through.

421
00:29:08,790 --> 00:29:09,580
Cut!

422
00:29:12,360 --> 00:29:15,250
I can overlook the fact that
your physique isn’t quite on my level.

423
00:29:15,590 --> 00:29:16,900
But I can’t overlook
you memorizing your lines

424
00:29:16,930 --> 00:29:17,970
without understanding them.

425
00:29:17,990 --> 00:29:19,600
This is the scene where we met.

426
00:29:19,660 --> 00:29:21,490
I hadn’t fallen for Lookpeach yet.

427
00:29:21,590 --> 00:29:22,660
So what are you two doing?

428
00:29:23,000 --> 00:29:25,770
You’re giving each other heart eyes
like a pair of lovers.

429
00:29:26,370 --> 00:29:27,100
Or what?

430
00:29:27,340 --> 00:29:30,090
Did sparks fly,
or are you two secretly in love?

431
00:29:30,960 --> 00:29:31,900
-No, sir.
-No, sir.

432
00:29:33,880 --> 00:29:34,780
We just…

433
00:29:35,250 --> 00:29:38,200
We prepared really hard.

434
00:29:38,230 --> 00:29:39,130
Prepared?!

435
00:29:40,070 --> 00:29:44,290
Was that really how two strangers
look at each other?

436
00:29:45,360 --> 00:29:46,200
Eccentric!

437
00:29:46,730 --> 00:29:50,110
We interpreted that,
in this scene, you both felt…

438
00:29:50,150 --> 00:29:51,100
Felt what?

439
00:29:51,700 --> 00:29:52,500
Huh?

440
00:29:53,320 --> 00:30:00,300
Felt the love at first sight, sir.

441
00:30:07,390 --> 00:30:08,500
So you’re saying

442
00:30:09,820 --> 00:30:12,100
Lookpeach fell for me at first sight?

443
00:30:19,290 --> 00:30:20,500
Is that right, Mr. Peach?

444
00:30:21,880 --> 00:30:22,700
No.

445
00:30:24,560 --> 00:30:28,000
I was scared of him,
and I couldn’t stand him.

446
00:30:32,750 --> 00:30:33,500
Switch!

447
00:30:33,800 --> 00:30:35,200
Switch to the next scene?

448
00:30:35,400 --> 00:30:36,300
Switch the actors.

449
00:30:38,330 --> 00:30:39,530
You’re not even wearing the contacts.

450
00:30:41,090 --> 00:30:42,550
-Mr. Thee!
-Mr. Thee has gray eyes.

451
00:30:42,580 --> 00:30:43,400
Mr. Thee!

452
00:30:43,430 --> 00:30:45,250
Why aren’t you wearing the contacts?

453
00:30:45,270 --> 00:30:46,330
My eyes are too small.

454
00:30:53,870 --> 00:30:55,850
You can touch me. I give you permission.

455
00:30:58,540 --> 00:31:00,700
Can you please stay in my sight forever?

456
00:31:03,490 --> 00:31:04,200
Keep rolling!

457
00:31:05,510 --> 00:31:07,180
(Actor-Doctor Jimmy.)

458
00:31:07,280 --> 00:31:10,500
One change required.
Instead of “please,” say “pwease.”

459
00:31:11,030 --> 00:31:11,800
Pwease?

460
00:31:12,370 --> 00:31:13,700
Pwease!

461
00:31:17,750 --> 00:31:18,710
Okay, sir. Sure.

462
00:31:18,860 --> 00:31:19,700
Okay. Again.

463
00:31:19,880 --> 00:31:21,580
And… action.

464
00:31:23,060 --> 00:31:25,180
You can touch me. I give you permission.

465
00:31:26,170 --> 00:31:28,300
Can you stay in my sight forever?

466
00:31:28,700 --> 00:31:29,600
Pwease?

467
00:31:29,960 --> 00:31:31,300
You’re the only one…

468
00:31:32,310 --> 00:31:33,970
who wants me around for a long time.

469
00:31:37,510 --> 00:31:39,330
Am I your one and only too?

470
00:31:40,500 --> 00:31:43,180
Hey, you should be careful.

471
00:31:44,000 --> 00:31:46,500
Not everyone will try to interpret
what you mean.

472
00:31:47,530 --> 00:31:49,180
Luckily, I—

473
00:31:49,240 --> 00:31:50,730
Then I guess I like you.

474
00:31:54,440 --> 00:31:55,180
(Cut!)

475
00:31:59,150 --> 00:32:00,600
A man like Theerakit Kian Lee,

476
00:32:01,570 --> 00:32:02,950
who’s hot, brilliant,
and ridiculously handsome,

477
00:32:02,970 --> 00:32:04,010
says he likes you,

478
00:32:04,180 --> 00:32:05,800
and that’s all the reaction you’ve got?

479
00:32:06,290 --> 00:32:07,210
I’m sorry, Mr. Thee.

480
00:32:07,450 --> 00:32:08,200
Again!

481
00:32:19,930 --> 00:32:22,600
And… action!

482
00:32:24,470 --> 00:32:26,000
Then I guess I like you.

483
00:32:32,100 --> 00:32:33,400
I need more emotion.

484
00:32:38,260 --> 00:32:39,580
More stunned.

485
00:32:42,960 --> 00:32:44,070
More shocked.

486
00:32:47,090 --> 00:32:48,090
(Now you look scary.)

487
00:32:48,370 --> 00:32:50,380
I want awe.

488
00:32:52,500 --> 00:32:53,600
(“Oh, wow.”)

489
00:32:53,980 --> 00:32:55,300
“Someone confessed to me.”

490
00:32:58,600 --> 00:32:59,680
(You’re deeply moved.)

491
00:33:00,450 --> 00:33:01,800
You’re this close to tears.

492
00:33:04,750 --> 00:33:06,090
Blink twice.

493
00:33:08,440 --> 00:33:09,760
Was I really like that?

494
00:33:11,660 --> 00:33:12,900
I don’t think this is accurate.

495
00:33:13,200 --> 00:33:14,050
Don’t you like it, Lookpeach?

496
00:33:17,110 --> 00:33:17,700
Switch!

497
00:33:17,720 --> 00:33:18,850
-Switch the acting style?
-Switch what, sir?

498
00:33:18,970 --> 00:33:19,970
Switch the actors.

499
00:33:20,840 --> 00:33:22,600
Mr. Thee! Can I have one more take?

500
00:33:22,760 --> 00:33:23,690
I want to be in this series.

501
00:33:24,000 --> 00:33:25,900
You can’t even blink twice.

502
00:33:25,950 --> 00:33:27,270
But I did.

503
00:33:27,420 --> 00:33:28,570
No means no!

504
00:33:28,870 --> 00:33:29,980
(Replace the whole cast!)

505
00:33:30,620 --> 00:33:31,800
“I do not act on impulse!”

506
00:33:33,880 --> 00:33:34,780
I do not act on impulse!

507
00:33:36,370 --> 00:33:37,800
-That’s not enough.
-Yes, sir.

508
00:33:37,980 --> 00:33:39,280
You need to shake more.

509
00:33:39,310 --> 00:33:40,620
-More?
-Watch carefully.

510
00:33:42,420 --> 00:33:43,700
“I do not act on impulse!”

511
00:33:44,720 --> 00:33:45,580
I do not act on impulse!

512
00:33:45,610 --> 00:33:46,400
Stop!

513
00:33:51,940 --> 00:33:53,500
-I do not act on impulse!
-I do not act on impulse!

514
00:33:53,600 --> 00:33:54,500
Your voice is too deep.

515
00:33:54,530 --> 00:33:56,060
-I do not act on impulse!
-I do not act on impulse!

516
00:33:56,110 --> 00:33:56,980
I do not act on impulse!

517
00:33:57,070 --> 00:33:57,970
I do not act on impulse!

518
00:33:58,010 --> 00:33:59,400
I do not act on impulse!!

519
00:33:59,470 --> 00:34:00,230
That’s too furious.

520
00:34:00,280 --> 00:34:01,300
I do not act on impulse!

521
00:34:01,820 --> 00:34:03,730
Brrr. I do not act on impulse!

522
00:34:03,800 --> 00:34:05,810
I do not act on impulse!!!

523
00:34:05,860 --> 00:34:06,500
Jeez!

524
00:34:07,910 --> 00:34:09,000
Can we shoot already?

525
00:34:09,270 --> 00:34:10,770
Mark waited so long he fell asleep.

526
00:34:13,880 --> 00:34:14,699
I do not act on impulse.

527
00:34:14,850 --> 00:34:17,400
-I do not act on impulse
-We’re two hours late.

528
00:34:19,300 --> 00:34:21,000
You’ve crushed my heart into pieces.

529
00:34:21,030 --> 00:34:22,449
You’ve done it, Peachayarat.

530
00:34:23,170 --> 00:34:25,500
I’m hurting to the point of dying.

531
00:34:25,770 --> 00:34:26,500
Huh?

532
00:34:32,110 --> 00:34:33,850
I keep repeating it to you
from morning to night

533
00:34:33,870 --> 00:34:36,500
that you will be safe under my care!

534
00:34:36,699 --> 00:34:38,250
And you still think of
running away from me?

535
00:34:38,969 --> 00:34:39,800
Hear me out.

536
00:34:39,949 --> 00:34:40,780
Remember this!

537
00:34:41,139 --> 00:34:43,179
Not even death can take you away from me!

538
00:34:43,250 --> 00:34:46,530
If Hell or Heaven has anyone
from the Lee family there,

539
00:34:46,620 --> 00:34:49,330
I’ll have my ancestors lock you away

540
00:34:50,090 --> 00:34:52,600
until the day I die and fall after you!

541
00:34:53,080 --> 00:34:53,690
Cut!

542
00:34:54,170 --> 00:34:54,929
Yes?

543
00:34:58,200 --> 00:35:00,400
I would never grab Lookpeach that roughly.

544
00:35:01,080 --> 00:35:01,800
Huh?

545
00:35:02,990 --> 00:35:05,300
If anyone’s going to hurt Lookpeach,

546
00:35:07,500 --> 00:35:10,200
remember that I, Theerakit Kian Lee,

547
00:35:11,040 --> 00:35:13,090
will be the last person on Earth to do it.

548
00:35:14,430 --> 00:35:15,210
Switch!

549
00:35:15,740 --> 00:35:16,620
Mr. Thee…

550
00:35:16,680 --> 00:35:17,980
Please, sir.

551
00:35:18,750 --> 00:35:19,750
I’ll lock you away

552
00:35:21,060 --> 00:35:23,200
until the day I die and fall after you!

553
00:35:24,770 --> 00:35:26,000
Did that work, Mr. Thee?

554
00:35:34,180 --> 00:35:35,000
Mr. Thee.

555
00:35:37,560 --> 00:35:38,200
Peach.

556
00:35:40,750 --> 00:35:42,200
How about we try dating?

557
00:35:45,650 --> 00:35:46,930
What did you say?

558
00:35:47,350 --> 00:35:49,690
I might be pretty busy with work,

559
00:35:50,280 --> 00:35:52,600
but I promise I’ll take good care of you.

560
00:35:54,130 --> 00:35:56,200
Whatever you want to do, just tell me.

561
00:35:57,700 --> 00:35:58,900
I’ll make it happen.

562
00:36:00,810 --> 00:36:03,800
If you like working,
I won’t get in your way.

563
00:36:06,240 --> 00:36:08,090
I’ll let you live your life.

564
00:36:10,060 --> 00:36:13,600
And don’t worry.
ARSENI won’t complicate your life.

565
00:36:17,210 --> 00:36:18,660
The world I’m about to build

566
00:36:19,490 --> 00:36:21,200
will be just the two of us.

567
00:36:26,960 --> 00:36:27,700
(Cut!)

568
00:36:32,920 --> 00:36:34,200
You don’t look nearly in love enough.

569
00:36:34,210 --> 00:36:34,760
But I—

570
00:36:35,000 --> 00:36:36,330
-In that moment…
-Yes?

571
00:36:38,080 --> 00:36:40,780
You should feel like
you’d gladly lay your heart at his feet.

572
00:36:41,330 --> 00:36:41,980
Get up.

573
00:36:42,300 --> 00:36:43,000
Get up! Get up!

574
00:36:43,030 --> 00:36:43,700
Yes, sir.

575
00:36:44,510 --> 00:36:45,150
Yes.

576
00:36:45,920 --> 00:36:46,780
Oh…

577
00:36:46,840 --> 00:36:47,600
Yes?

578
00:36:49,730 --> 00:36:50,380
Oh!

579
00:36:54,870 --> 00:36:55,800
And don’t worry.

580
00:36:57,290 --> 00:36:59,600
ARSENI won’t complicate your life.

581
00:37:00,050 --> 00:37:01,600
The world I’m about to build

582
00:37:03,580 --> 00:37:05,100
will be just the two of us.

583
00:37:06,300 --> 00:37:06,900
Cut!

584
00:37:11,660 --> 00:37:13,100
I haven’t said “Action” yet.

585
00:37:14,560 --> 00:37:15,500
But you can say “Cut.”

586
00:37:26,350 --> 00:37:27,800
Morning, noon, and night…

587
00:37:28,310 --> 00:37:30,200
I keep telling you I love only you.

588
00:37:30,740 --> 00:37:33,250
I believe you, but…

589
00:37:38,920 --> 00:37:39,580
I’m jealous.

590
00:37:39,680 --> 00:37:40,400
Jealous?

591
00:37:44,310 --> 00:37:45,580
You’re jealous, Lookpeach?

592
00:37:53,340 --> 00:37:57,900
I’m just not used to
seeing you so close to other people.

593
00:37:58,980 --> 00:38:00,300
I swear on my life…

594
00:38:01,180 --> 00:38:02,100
from now on,

595
00:38:02,870 --> 00:38:05,800
your eyes will never have to witness me
getting close to anyone else again.

596
00:38:07,250 --> 00:38:08,100
Don’t.

597
00:38:09,100 --> 00:38:11,060
I’ll fix my own jealousy by not going—

598
00:38:11,090 --> 00:38:12,600
It’s easier to fix something else.

599
00:38:13,290 --> 00:38:14,250
What?

600
00:38:14,910 --> 00:38:16,200
I fired them.

601
00:38:17,630 --> 00:38:18,800
Both of them.

602
00:38:29,790 --> 00:38:35,570
Is it true that you two turned down
the casting call for our series?

603
00:38:42,360 --> 00:38:43,300
Well…

604
00:38:44,100 --> 00:38:47,850
We read the script,
and we didn’t think we could pull it off.

605
00:38:48,890 --> 00:38:52,400
Besides, it’s been a while
since I’ve been around cameras.

606
00:38:53,560 --> 00:38:55,900
I’m afraid…

607
00:38:55,920 --> 00:38:56,800
Hah!

608
00:38:59,860 --> 00:39:01,500
More people are dying for these roles…

609
00:39:02,200 --> 00:39:04,500
than there are grains of sand
in the desert.

610
00:39:04,540 --> 00:39:06,090
So don’t even think…

611
00:39:07,650 --> 00:39:10,450
I asked you here so I could beg—

612
00:39:10,520 --> 00:39:11,500
I’m begging you.

613
00:39:12,820 --> 00:39:14,290
Please audition for the series.

614
00:39:14,510 --> 00:39:15,300
But…

615
00:39:19,800 --> 00:39:21,400
Not only did you refuse
to help row the boat,

616
00:39:22,570 --> 00:39:24,100
you ran straight back to shore.

617
00:39:30,920 --> 00:39:31,900
We really can’t.

618
00:39:40,050 --> 00:39:41,400
I thought you said it was dangerous.

619
00:39:42,400 --> 00:39:43,570
Aren’t you scared anymore?

620
00:39:44,520 --> 00:39:45,570
I was just saying that.

621
00:39:46,670 --> 00:39:48,170
Otherwise, I couldn’t
be with you, Mr. Thee.

622
00:39:52,310 --> 00:39:53,930
What did you just call me?

623
00:39:56,380 --> 00:39:58,000
I said it out of habit.

624
00:39:58,380 --> 00:40:00,200
Then you have to practice
until you’re used to it.

625
00:40:01,170 --> 00:40:04,900
Try calling me P’Kian.

626
00:40:05,990 --> 00:40:07,000
P’Kian.

627
00:40:10,980 --> 00:40:11,900
That’s so good.

628
00:40:13,840 --> 00:40:14,800
I love it.

629
00:40:20,050 --> 00:40:20,800
Cut.

630
00:40:22,270 --> 00:40:22,930
I’m sorry.

631
00:40:23,410 --> 00:40:24,800
Alright, guys. Let’s try again.

632
00:40:25,050 --> 00:40:25,730
Action!

633
00:40:26,230 --> 00:40:27,200
That’s so good.

634
00:40:28,470 --> 00:40:29,200
I love…

635
00:40:32,930 --> 00:40:34,100
I’m sorry. Sorry.

636
00:40:34,970 --> 00:40:35,980
Can they even do it?

637
00:40:36,970 --> 00:40:37,660
(Cut!)

638
00:40:38,580 --> 00:40:39,900
P’Kian.

639
00:40:41,980 --> 00:40:42,650
(Cut!)

640
00:40:42,880 --> 00:40:43,900
P’Kian!

641
00:40:50,580 --> 00:40:51,450
Mr. Thee’s watching.

642
00:40:51,860 --> 00:40:52,670
P’Kian.

643
00:40:52,760 --> 00:40:53,330
(Cut.)

644
00:40:53,360 --> 00:40:54,430
P’Kian.

645
00:40:54,500 --> 00:40:55,090
(Cut.)

646
00:40:55,270 --> 00:40:56,800
P’Kian! Was that okay?

647
00:40:57,040 --> 00:40:57,570
(Cut.)

648
00:40:58,060 --> 00:40:58,780
I’m sorry.

649
00:40:58,840 --> 00:40:59,900
P’Kian!

650
00:41:03,080 --> 00:41:03,700
Cut.

651
00:41:04,260 --> 00:41:05,100
P’Kian.

652
00:41:08,160 --> 00:41:10,540
Cut!!

653
00:41:14,540 --> 00:41:15,200
I’m sorry.

654
00:41:16,350 --> 00:41:17,500
It’s okay.

655
00:41:17,860 --> 00:41:18,800
I understand.

656
00:41:19,660 --> 00:41:20,800
The dialogue is…

657
00:41:23,550 --> 00:41:24,410
weird.

658
00:41:27,800 --> 00:41:30,200
I’m sorry for wasting your time.

659
00:41:30,710 --> 00:41:32,930
Is that really how you two
talk to each other?

660
00:41:38,010 --> 00:41:43,290
Ah! Should we rewrite the script
to make you sound more like normal people?

661
00:41:43,930 --> 00:41:46,300
Keep it simple.

662
00:41:46,920 --> 00:41:47,750
Simple?

663
00:41:48,960 --> 00:41:50,100
Why would I make it simple?

664
00:41:50,550 --> 00:41:52,780
I hate that word more than anything.

665
00:41:56,790 --> 00:41:59,410
Your lives are perfect and extraordinary.

666
00:41:59,800 --> 00:42:02,100
Who else could ever handle Mr. Thee
the way you do, Peach?

667
00:42:02,150 --> 00:42:03,580
No one could take the roles.

668
00:42:03,810 --> 00:42:07,130
Should we put the project on hold for now?

669
00:42:14,630 --> 00:42:15,730
Or maybe…

670
00:42:24,690 --> 00:42:25,600
Honestly,

671
00:42:26,350 --> 00:42:28,780
I think one of the dreams
most photographers have

672
00:42:29,120 --> 00:42:31,200
is owning their own gallery.

673
00:42:31,890 --> 00:42:33,200
It’s certainly one of mine.

674
00:42:34,410 --> 00:42:37,180
And today, I finally
made that dream come true.

675
00:42:37,710 --> 00:42:39,590
Oh, no.

676
00:42:40,390 --> 00:42:41,400
He made it come true for me.

677
00:42:41,650 --> 00:42:43,780
Mr. Peach, isn’t the one
you’re talking about

678
00:42:43,800 --> 00:42:48,400
also the theme
of this venue’s first exhibition?

679
00:42:50,110 --> 00:42:50,900
That’s right.

680
00:42:51,980 --> 00:42:55,410
Can you tell us the inspiration
behind this exhibition?

681
00:42:56,780 --> 00:42:58,500
I love taking his picture.

682
00:42:59,500 --> 00:43:00,650
Especially when he smiles.

683
00:43:02,340 --> 00:43:05,800
As you know,
Mr. Theerakit built this place,

684
00:43:06,690 --> 00:43:09,250
so I wanted to do something
to give back to him.

685
00:43:11,680 --> 00:43:13,600
And he’s handsome.

686
00:43:14,080 --> 00:43:15,100
Very handsome, in fact.

687
00:43:15,620 --> 00:43:16,900
I don’t want to keep that all to myself.

688
00:43:24,490 --> 00:43:27,580
Actually, the concept of this exhibition
is very simple.

689
00:43:30,700 --> 00:43:35,100
It’s about my journey and how I’ve grown.

690
00:43:37,680 --> 00:43:39,000
The journey includes everyone,

691
00:43:39,360 --> 00:43:40,500
not just Mr. Thee.

692
00:43:43,010 --> 00:43:43,800
Cold?

693
00:43:45,290 --> 00:43:46,900
I don’t like washing my hair.

694
00:43:47,770 --> 00:43:49,610
That’s why I told you to just stay still.

695
00:43:51,750 --> 00:43:52,300
Ow!

696
00:43:52,960 --> 00:43:53,920
I got it in my eye.

697
00:43:53,940 --> 00:43:54,900
I’m sorry.

698
00:44:06,600 --> 00:44:10,000
Without them,
I wouldn’t be where I am today.

699
00:44:11,430 --> 00:44:13,900
Could you move a little closer to him?

700
00:44:22,120 --> 00:44:25,800
There are a few people
I want to keep in my life forever.

701
00:44:29,230 --> 00:44:31,900
Mr. Peach, could you please elaborate?

702
00:44:34,410 --> 00:44:35,800
I don’t have many friends.

703
00:44:37,530 --> 00:44:39,580
And I don’t know many people, either.

704
00:44:48,100 --> 00:44:49,900
Today’s the announcement
of the new leader.

705
00:44:53,440 --> 00:44:54,800
I hope today’s your day.

706
00:44:56,150 --> 00:45:01,900
What I want… is to keep them in my life.

707
00:45:08,970 --> 00:45:11,900
I, Theerakit Kian Lee,

708
00:45:12,600 --> 00:45:15,100
promise to love

709
00:45:16,090 --> 00:45:17,000
and…

710
00:45:21,200 --> 00:45:23,000
Gosh, I need to say it more firmly.

711
00:45:24,800 --> 00:45:27,100
I, Theerakit Kian Lee,

712
00:45:27,360 --> 00:45:31,100
promise to love and be faithful to you

713
00:45:31,820 --> 00:45:33,900
in good times and in bad,

714
00:45:34,730 --> 00:45:37,400
in sickness and in health.

715
00:45:40,770 --> 00:45:43,500
Congratulations, Mr. Master Photographer.

716
00:45:51,590 --> 00:45:53,500
How many continents
did these flowers come from?

717
00:45:55,760 --> 00:45:59,120
Ever since I met you,
I’ve learned something.

718
00:45:59,630 --> 00:46:02,000
No matter how hard
you search for the very best,

719
00:46:03,490 --> 00:46:05,500
nothing compares to
what’s already right in front of you.

720
00:46:14,870 --> 00:46:16,500
It’s only one kind of flower.

721
00:46:17,080 --> 00:46:18,300
The Peach Blossom.

722
00:46:19,220 --> 00:46:20,500
For my special one.

723
00:46:25,370 --> 00:46:26,000
Ahem.

724
00:46:28,570 --> 00:46:29,900
Don’t just smell the flowers.

725
00:46:31,480 --> 00:46:33,090
Give the man who brought them a kiss too.

726
00:46:54,310 --> 00:46:55,180
Overjoyed.

727
00:47:01,440 --> 00:47:03,410
You stood in front of this photo
for quite a while.

728
00:47:04,520 --> 00:47:05,600
What were you thinking about?

729
00:47:06,610 --> 00:47:07,900
I was remembering that day.

730
00:47:09,470 --> 00:47:14,900
Do you realize you’ve kept every promise
you ever made to me?

731
00:47:15,300 --> 00:47:16,100
I do.

732
00:47:17,740 --> 00:47:20,490
Because I want this
to be the greatest love there is.

733
00:47:21,000 --> 00:47:21,810
Thank you…

734
00:47:23,560 --> 00:47:27,000
for making my world just the two of us.

735
00:47:30,030 --> 00:47:31,130
Just me…

736
00:47:32,160 --> 00:47:33,100
and Thee.

737
00:47:37,940 --> 00:47:39,220
My world too.

738
00:47:40,640 --> 00:47:43,400
There’s only Peach and me.

739
00:48:33,540 --> 00:48:35,800
(This is the story of the two of you.)

740
00:48:36,320 --> 00:48:40,610
(I don't think anyone could tell it
better than the people who lived it.)

741
00:48:41,040 --> 00:48:41,900
(Trust me.)

742
00:48:42,060 --> 00:48:44,650
Hello, and thank you
to all the lovely members of the press.

743
00:48:44,880 --> 00:48:47,980
How much do I have to pay
to make your front page?

744
00:48:48,120 --> 00:48:50,650
I apologize on his behalf, everyone.

745
00:48:53,200 --> 00:48:55,590
Congrats on your show, bro.

746
00:48:55,620 --> 00:48:57,580
Sorry I missed your press con.

747
00:48:57,610 --> 00:49:00,200
I’ve been busy…

748
00:49:00,810 --> 00:49:01,900
Busy loving my boyfriend.

749
00:49:03,700 --> 00:49:04,780
Busy with work.

750
00:49:05,790 --> 00:49:07,600
Congratulations again,
Mr. Thee and Mr. Peach.

751
00:49:08,490 --> 00:49:09,370
Congrats!

752
00:49:09,900 --> 00:49:10,770
(Bye-bye.)

753
00:49:11,420 --> 00:49:12,300
(Bye-bye.)

754
00:49:12,970 --> 00:49:13,850
(Bye.)

755
00:49:16,140 --> 00:49:17,200
Wow.

756
00:49:17,500 --> 00:49:21,000
We’ve heard from the little brother
and the best friend.

757
00:49:21,030 --> 00:49:23,600
Now let’s hear from
the big brother himself.

758
00:49:23,830 --> 00:49:24,850
Mr. Theerakit,

759
00:49:25,180 --> 00:49:30,300
now that you’ve watched the first episode
of Me and Thee with everyone,

760
00:49:30,430 --> 00:49:31,700
how do you feel?

761
00:49:31,880 --> 00:49:33,290
Thank you all for coming.

762
00:49:33,360 --> 00:49:36,170
To repay you, we’ve prepared
a bottle of Peach and Me perfume

763
00:49:36,320 --> 00:49:37,600
under each of your seats,

764
00:49:37,620 --> 00:49:39,650
along with an international buffet

765
00:49:40,500 --> 00:49:42,900
inspired by the countries
we visited on our honeymoon.

766
00:49:43,180 --> 00:49:46,890
Please fill your stomach
to your heart’s content after the event.

767
00:49:48,280 --> 00:49:50,570
What about you, Mr. Peach?
How do you feel?

768
00:49:50,920 --> 00:49:53,100
Thank you all for joining us.

769
00:49:53,320 --> 00:49:55,490
At first, we just wanted
to make this series for fun.

770
00:49:55,650 --> 00:49:56,900
Something to remember.

771
00:49:57,320 --> 00:50:02,000
I hope the ARSENAI fandom enjoys it.

772
00:50:03,670 --> 00:50:04,760
ARSENAI!

773
00:50:04,800 --> 00:50:06,700
ARSENI!

774
00:50:07,200 --> 00:50:08,090
ARSENAI!

775
00:50:08,370 --> 00:50:10,460
ARSENI!

776
00:50:10,490 --> 00:50:11,600
Awesome!

777
00:50:11,800 --> 00:50:12,500
Whoo!

778
00:50:17,090 --> 00:50:19,300
Let’s move on to our last question.

779
00:50:19,450 --> 00:50:24,850
This series is based on the true story
of Mr. Thee and Mr. Peach.

780
00:50:24,930 --> 00:50:31,700
Fans have been saying
your lives should be on a reality show.

781
00:50:31,990 --> 00:50:34,200
Would you be interested, Mr. Peach?

782
00:50:34,590 --> 00:50:36,610
I think one series is enough.

783
00:50:36,920 --> 00:50:39,240
Oh, come on.

784
00:50:39,700 --> 00:50:42,980
But the ARSENAIs would love it.

785
00:50:43,010 --> 00:50:43,900
Enough!

786
00:50:46,130 --> 00:50:47,300
He’s my Lookpeach.

787
00:50:48,270 --> 00:50:49,700
I’m keeping him all to myself.

788
00:50:58,790 --> 00:51:00,570
THE(E) END
FOR REAL THIS TIME

789
00:51:00,760 --> 00:51:02,100
You’re jealous, Lookpeach?

790
00:51:05,610 --> 00:51:06,690
Let’s try that again.

791
00:51:07,020 --> 00:51:08,800
Brrr! I do not act on impulse!!

792
00:51:10,350 --> 00:51:11,500
Because I…

793
00:51:12,130 --> 00:51:13,600
will make me, nope!

794
00:51:14,230 --> 00:51:15,000
What am I saying?

795
00:51:16,200 --> 00:51:17,000
Your eyelash.

796
00:51:17,440 --> 00:51:18,600
♪ Take it, take it off ♪

797
00:51:21,350 --> 00:51:21,900
Don’t!

798
00:51:22,290 --> 00:51:23,500
That’s my partner’s little sister!

799
00:51:25,450 --> 00:51:26,210
Why laugh?

800
00:51:26,230 --> 00:51:27,350
Sorry. Can we do it again?

801
00:51:27,800 --> 00:51:29,170
It’s like they were playing something.
